# CLAUDE.md - Household Finance Agent

Personal finance app for Alex and Addison. Replaces EveryDollar with a self-hosted budget tracker plus cash-flow projection and a daily 7am email brief. This file is the build spec; every decision below was made with Alex in September 2026. Do not re-litigate decisions, but ask when something is genuinely ambiguous.

## Style rule

Never use em dashes in any generated writing, emails, or UI copy.

## Stack (decided)

- Node.js + Express on Railway, Postgres (Railway plugin). Same stack as Alex's FreePro app.
- One deployable service containing: REST API, cron jobs, and a mobile-friendly web UI.
- Make.com watches the email inbox and POSTs parsed bank-notification transactions to this app. Make owns nothing; this app owns all data.
- Email out via Resend (or SendGrid). Claude API (model claude-sonnet-4-6) writes the daily narrative and is the auto-coding fallback.
- Balances are seeded manually and carried forward by the app. Reconciled each budget period. Plaid is a later upgrade, not now.

## Files in this handoff

- `schema.sql`: full Postgres schema plus seed data (accounts, recurring items, budget periods, categories, coding rules table). Run once on a fresh database.
- `budgets_seed.sql`: 6 fiscal months of category budgets converted from Alex's EveryDollar CSVs. Run after schema.sql.
- `engine.js`: the projection engine, a pure function, already tested. Feed it rows from Postgres. Supports pay_full_balance, pay_period_charges (with initial_accrual), reserves, and flags.
- `run-projection.js`: test harness with real seed data and documented assumptions. Keep as a regression test.

## Household model (all decided, do not change without asking Alex)

- Fiscal months run the 15th through the 14th. EveryDollar exports are named by END month: "10-2026" = Sep 15 to Oct 14.
- Income: Alex ~$2,000 every Friday (Kenna Group, started Sept 2026). Addison $2,500 every other Wednesday anchored 2026-09-16 (Edward Jones; her 9/2 first check was $3,697.88 pre-deductions). Family childcare support $1,200 on the 1st via Venmo (lands in Spending 4815, gets transferred to Bills 5061; the daily email should nudge this transfer around the 1st). DCA reimbursement $625/month, requested on the 6th, continues under Edward Jones benefits.
