## What to build (in order)

### 1. App scaffold + migrations
Express app, pg client, migration runner that applies schema.sql then budgets_seed.sql. Environment: DATABASE_URL, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, RESEND_API_KEY, INGEST_SECRET, TZ=America/Chicago.

### 2. Ingestion endpoint for Make.com
POST /api/ingest with header X-Ingest-Secret. Body: {account_last4, date, amount, description, external_ref}. Signed amount, negative = money out. Upsert on (account_id, external_ref) so Make retries are safe. On insert, run auto-coding (step 3) and update the running balance. Return 200 with {id, category, balance}.

### 3. Auto-coding
Layer 1: coding_rules table, case-insensitive substring match on description, lowest priority number wins. Seed obvious rules (ALDI -> Groceries, MSD -> Sewer, AT&T -> AT&T, SOFI -> Sofi, etc.) from the category list. Layer 2: no rule match -> one Claude API call with the description, amount, account, and the category list; response must be JSON {category, confidence}. Store which layer coded it. Layer 3: when Alex re-codes a transaction in the UI, write a new coding_rule (created_from='correction') so the same merchant never needs Claude again.

### 4. Budget UI (EveryDollar replacement)
Mobile-first single page. Current fiscal period by default with a period switcher. Groups and line items exactly as in categories: planned, spent (sum of coded transactions in period), remaining, with progress bars. Income section shows received vs planned. A transactions list with tap-to-recode. Show Bills balance vs the $8,100 reserve prominently. Keep it fast and plain; no build framework needed, server-rendered plus a little vanilla JS is fine.

### 5. Projection integration
Nightly (and on demand) run engine.js with live balances and recurring_items. Store the 45-day result. Surface in the UI: low point and date, reserve dips, upcoming 7 days of bills.

### 6. Daily 7am email
Cron 06:45 America/Chicago. Compose data: current balances, projected low point and date, bills due in next 7 days, budget period status per group (planned vs spent vs remaining), reserve status, any flags (OVERDRAFT, RESERVE_DIP, LOW_BALANCE), and a recommended-transfers section (e.g. move the $1,200 Venmo to Bills near the 1st; suggest extra Southwest card payment when Bills exceeds reserve + buffer + upcoming 7-day outflows). Claude API writes a short plain-language narrative from that data. Send via Resend at 7:00. Subject: "Daily brief: [date]". No em dashes anywhere.

### 7. Notifications (after the above works)
On ingest of a deposit or any transaction over a threshold (default $200), send an immediate short email. Configurable per rule later; keep simple now.

